Resolve precompiled OS deps for the TARGET architecture, not the executor's.

`Bundlex.get_target/0` is what every Membrane plugin's bundlex.exs passes to
`Membrane.PrecompiledDependencyProvider.get_dependency_url/2`, and that function
picks `<dep>_linux_x86.tar.gz` vs `<dep>_linux_arm.tar.gz` from it. Without
CROSSCOMPILE set, `get_target/0` reads `:erlang.system_info(:system_architecture)`
-- the triple of the BEAM running the build, i.e. the RBE executor. Building for
linux/arm64 therefore asked for `srtp_linux_x86.tar.gz`, missed the staged
`srtp_linux_arm.tar.gz` in BUNDLEX_LOCAL_PRECOMPILED_DIR (matching is by
basename), downloaded the x86 archive from github at build time, and died with
    ld.lld: error: .../libsrtp2.so is incompatible with aarch64linux
This is the same shape of bug as lazy_html, adbc and mdex_native: an
architecture-keyed artefact resolved from the build host rather than the target.

Bundlex already has the override -- the `{:ok, _crosscompile}` branch below reads
TARGET_ARCH/TARGET_VENDOR/TARGET_OS/TARGET_ABI, the Nerves cross-compilation
convention that cc_precompiler and rustler_precompiled honour too, and which
//build:mix_app.bzl exports for every linux-target Mix action. It is unreachable
here: setting CROSSCOMPILE also flips `Bundlex.Platform.get_target!/0` to
`:custom`, which swaps Toolchain.GCC for Toolchain.Custom and changes far more
than the triple (see hermetic_cc.patch).

So read the same four variables in the non-CROSSCOMPILE branch, keeping
`:erlang.system_info/1` as the fallback when they are absent. The platform, the
toolchain and every non-Bazel build are untouched: mix_app exports TARGET_ARCH
only when the target platform is Linux, so a macOS or plain `mix` build takes the
original path unchanged.

--- a/lib/bundlex.ex
+++ b/lib/bundlex.ex
@@ -43,15 +43,26 @@
         end
       else
         def get_target() do
-          [architecture, vendor, os | maybe_abi] =
-            :erlang.system_info(:system_architecture) |> List.to_string() |> String.split("-")
+          case System.get_env("TARGET_ARCH") do
+            nil ->
+              [architecture, vendor, os | maybe_abi] =
+                :erlang.system_info(:system_architecture) |> List.to_string() |> String.split("-")
 
-          %{
-            architecture: architecture,
-            vendor: vendor,
-            os: os,
-            abi: List.first(maybe_abi) || "unknown"
-          }
+              %{
+                architecture: architecture,
+                vendor: vendor,
+                os: os,
+                abi: List.first(maybe_abi) || "unknown"
+              }
+
+            architecture ->
+              %{
+                architecture: architecture,
+                vendor: System.get_env("TARGET_VENDOR", "unknown"),
+                os: System.get_env("TARGET_OS", "unknown"),
+                abi: System.get_env("TARGET_ABI", "unknown")
+              }
+          end
         end
       end
 
